Description: Take pictures at the camera's full resolution
 Snapshot takes pictures from its viewfinder stream, which aperture keeps at
 the largest height up to 1080.  For a 4128x3096 sensor behind libcamera's
 software ISP that is 1280x1080, so every picture was 1280x1080.
 .
 In picture mode the viewfinder now streams the camera's largest raw size,
 and a picture is the next frame of that stream.  Video mode keeps the
 1080p-class size used for recording.  Switching mode restarts the stream
 once.
 .
 A camerabin still capture at a larger size was not used: wrappercamerabinsrc
 would renegotiate the source twice per picture and keep the first frame
 after the first restart, and libcamera's software IPA resets white balance
 and autofocus on every configure.
 .
 pipewiresrc 1.0 restarts the camera for every RECONFIGURE event, and
 camerabin sends several per picture without changing the format.  A probe
 on the source's capsfilter drops those whose preferred caps are the caps in
 use, as pipewiresrc itself does from PipeWire 1.1.81 (e2e8cf79), so a
 picture no longer restarts the camera at all.
